## 2️⃣ `arcade/mind-chambers/focus-relay/focus-relay.cavecode`

```text
CAVECODE SPEC — FOCUS RELAY (ARC-MC-002)
Category: mind-chambers
Engine: visual sequence memory
Version: 1.1

============================================================
🪨 BLOCK 1 — IDENTITY
------------------------------------------------------------
Title: Mind Chambers — Focus Relay
Game ID: ARC-MC-002
Category: mind-chambers
Genre: sequence-memory / focus
One-Liner: Memorize the numbered flashes and click the nodes in the correct order.
(LOCKED)

============================================================
🎮 BLOCK 2 — CORE LOOP SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------
High-level loop:

  - STATE = IDLE
  - Player presses "Start Round" → generate pattern.

Round flow:

  1. Generate a unique set of grid cells of length patternLength.
  2. Enter REVEAL state:
       - For revealTimeMs, display numbers 1..patternLength on those cells.
       - After the timer expires, hide numbers and switch to INPUT state.
  3. INPUT state:
       - Wait for player clicks/taps.
       - Keep an index expectedIndex starting at 1.
       - When a node is clicked:
            - If that node corresponds to expectedIndex:
                  - Mark it as correct.
                  - Increment expectedIndex.
                  - If expectedIndex > patternLength:
                        - Round success → increment score.
                        - Increase patternLength and adjust revealTime.
                        - Enter TRANSITION for 650ms; ignore taps.
                        - Go back to REVEAL state for next round.
            - Else: mistake → GAME OVER.
  4. GAME OVER:
       - Show score, allow restarting from Round 1.

(LOCKED)

============================================================
🕹️ BLOCK 3 — INPUT / CONTROLS
------------------------------------------------------------
Desktop:
  - Mouse click on nodes during INPUT state.

Mobile:
  - Touch / tap on nodes during INPUT state.

The "Restart Run" button:
  - Starts a new run from Round 1 if in GAME OVER or IDLE.
  - Starts Round 1 if no run active yet.

(LOCKED)

============================================================
📈 BLOCK 4 — SCORING / PROGRESSION
------------------------------------------------------------
Score:
  - score = number of successfully completed rounds.

Progression:
  - patternLength starts at startPatternLength.
  - After each successful round:
        - patternLength = min(gridSize * gridSize, patternLength + patternIncrement)
        - revealTimeMs = max(minRevealTimeMs, revealTimeMs - revealTimeDecayMs)

The 3x3 board caps patterns at nine unique cells; rounds continue at that
capacity while reveal time decreases to its floor. Tiers: 3 cells = 1,
4-5 = 2, 6-7 = 3, 8 = 4, 9 = 5. Completion uses actual pattern length.
Each click is handled once by the board. Restart cancels reveal and
transition timers before generating a fresh run.

Game ends when:
  - Player clicks any node that is not the expected next index.

(LOCKED)

============================================================
🎚️ BLOCK 5 — TUNING KNOBS (HUMAN EDIT ZONE)
------------------------------------------------------------
gridSize:            3          # 3x3 grid
startPatternLength:  3
patternIncrement:    1
revealTimeMs:        1600
minRevealTimeMs:     700
revealTimeDecayMs:   100

(PENCIL — keep in sync with index.html script)

============================================================
🌐 BLOCK 6 — PLAYER-FACING TEXT
------------------------------------------------------------
title: "Focus Relay"
subtitle: "Remember the order. Tap it back."
startLabel: "Restart Run"
statusIdle: "Tap Restart Run to begin."
statusReveal: "Memorize the numbers..."
statusInput: "Tap the nodes in order."
statusRoundSuccess: "Nice. Get ready for the next pattern."
statusGameOver: "Sequence broken. Tap Restart Run to try again."
(Globe)

============================================================
🧩 BLOCK 7 — OPTIONAL EXPANSIONS
------------------------------------------------------------
